{"step_index":138,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-11-23T16:23:42Z","model":"gemini-3.8-flash-high","input_tokens":2461,"cache_read_tokens":64881,"output_tokens":1376,"thinking":"The JavaScript file (`stockfish.js`) is designed to run within a web worker. It attempts to load a WebAssembly binary (`stockfish.wasm`) at the same origin. Because both files are present in the same `public` directory, the WebAssembly version of Stockfish should be used for optimal performance through standard web worker messaging.\n\n\nThe main thread uses the Web Worker to execute UCI commands like `uci`, `setoption`, `isready`, and move commands. The worker then responds with UCI output, including `bestmove` which is parsed to extract the 'from', 'to', and possible promotion for use with the `chess.js` engine's `move` function. If 'bestmove' is '(none)', it indicates game over.\n\n\nFocus is on enhancing the user interface with visual cues and game controls for an improved chess-playing experience. Features include move highlighting, check/checkmate indicators, timer, difficulty settings, and move history for a more interactive presentation of the game. Implementation will involve integration with chess.js for rule enforcement and Stockfish.js for the AI engine, ensuring the UI remains responsive even when the engine is processing moves.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"cd 'C:\\\\Users\\\\DELL\\\\.gemini\\\\antigravity\\\\scratch\\\\stockfish-chess-arena'; node -e \\\"\\nconst rcb = require('react-chessboard');\\nconsole.log('react-chessboard exports:', Object.keys(rcb));\\n\\\"\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolSummary":"\"Check react-chessboard exports\""}}]}
